libmusiccast
============

C library and **mcctl** CLI for discovering and controlling Yamaha MusicCast
devices on your LAN using the Yamaha Extended Control (YXC) HTTP API.

Requirements
------------

* A UNIX-like system (Linux, macOS, MinGW, etc.)
* **Runtime:** libcurl, json-c
* **Build:** Autoconf, Automake, Libtool, pkg-config, a C compiler
* **Optional:** Check (unit tests), lcov/gcovr (coverage)

Compatible Yamaha MusicCast hardware on the same network as the machine running
mcctl or your application.

Quick start
-----------

From a release tarball:

  $ ./configure
  $ make
  $ sudo make install

From git:

  $ autoreconf -fi
  $ ./configure --enable-tests
  $ make
  $ make check

Try **mcctl detect**, then **mcctl HOST status** (or **mcctl -a HOST status**).
See **mcctl(1)** after install, or **mcctl help**.

API coverage
------------

See [docs/mcctl-api-coverage.md](docs/mcctl-api-coverage.md) for which YXC
endpoints are implemented. Official Yamaha spec PDFs are not included in the
repo; see [docs/YXC-specs.md](docs/YXC-specs.md).

